Engine: serialise during a screen's input delay (open fix 42).

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written and proved by work order 184 (Part 2),
parked for Data (doc/briefs/184-parked-for-data.md, item 1). No engine
patch may be applied in that order.

PROOF (work order 184, 27 September 2026): in a scratch clone of
orionlayer-local 4bf152e4 (never on orionlayer-local itself) this file
applied with `patch -p1 --dry-run` and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz,
and the applied tree equals the scratch commit; the scratch engine was
built in full with the linux-debug preset (ORION2RE_EXT=ON) — no error —
and a control, the same file with `MOX::_current_screen` misspelt
`MOX::_current_scren` in fields.cpp, was refused by the compiler. The
scratch engine then ran on the virtual display: see the entry,
doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 42.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch (after fix 41):

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_input_delay_tick.patch

then rebuild. It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    fields::Get_Input_() returns 0 while a screen's input delay runs
    (fields.cpp:161-164) and calls ext::Tick only after it (:167) — so
    while a delay counts down, nothing reaches a client: no state, no
    field list, no picture. The research panel sets a delay of five
    passes of 110 ms (tech.cpp:306, :349-351), and its list reached
    OrionLayer ~550 ms after the engine had built and drawn it — on every
    entry, 66-80 % of the time from the click to the panel (work order
    184, doc/briefs/184-research-timing.md). 42 call sites set a delay
    (1, 2, 3, 5 or 20 passes); every one of those screens is heard
    that much later.

    The change ticks during the delay too, and changes nothing else: the
    delay still returns 0 and still counts down, so the original ignores
    input for exactly as long as before; a field activation that arrives
    meanwhile waits in ext::g_pending_field, which is consumed only after
    the delay, as before. One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 42.`, on one
    line at the one changed place.

